# Control Magic gives the human the AI's Grizzly Bears (Layer 2). Lightning
# Bolt kills them: they go to the AI's graveyard, and a card leaving for a zone
# without a controller loses every controller but its owner
# (GameAction.java:671-673, Card.clearControllers). Java keeps a static's
# control in the same tempControllers it clears, so the Bears are no longer
# "YouCtrl" for the human: Raise Dead (Origin$ Graveyard | ValidTgts$
# Creature.YouCtrl) has no legal target and cannot be cast. With the static's
# control row left on the dead card, the human would raise the AI's Bears
# into the AI's hand.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 3 R
queue targets 2
castspell human 5
resolvestack
tapformana human 4 B
queue targets 2
castspell human 6
